# cuts/v1.0.45/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# WHY v1.0.45 EXISTS: Andy walked v1.0.44 on hardware 2026-08-24. It INSTALLED
# (fda_extract passed, scanned=30 third_party=2 missing=0, exactly the off-box
# prediction) but FAILED QA, and the headline was #876: install.sh announced
# "Doctor running http://localhost:8089" while com.ostler.doctor was NOT LOADED
# -- both launchctl attempts silenced, the chain ended `|| true`, and success
# was printed unconditionally. That one bug cascaded into most of the walk's
# other reds. This cut carries that fix and five siblings.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 DAEMON_COMMIT MOVES. DO NOT COPY v1.0.44's "UNCHANGED" LINE FORWARD.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.43 and v1.0.44 both pinned DAEMON_COMMIT=1b0a5013525a and v1.0.44's
# cut.env states, correctly for its own cut, that the daemon lane had not
# moved. It HAS now, and the thing that moved it is the fix Andy has named as
# his angriest item across ten DMGs.
#
# The wiki nav crop has TWO halves and they live in different repos:
#   CM044 6b0492d  emits ONE chrome band when embedded  (the wiki half)
#   oa    e83d1997 removes the host's 56px iframe crop  (the host half)
#
# The 56px was never covering "Andypedia" -- CM044 already hid its header when
# embedded, so the crop was eating the wiki's own TAB BAR: .md-header is 76.8px
# = __inner 38.4 + .md-tabs 38.4, so 56 lands 17.6px into the tabs and removes
# 45.9% of that row. Control with the crop at 0: 0.0%. That is why the nav
# looked clipped for ten DMGs while every wiki-side fix measured correct.
#
# MEASURED, both directions, before writing this line:
#   compare 1b0a5013525a...e83d1997  -> status=ahead  ahead_by=1 behind_by=0
#   compare e83d1997...1b0a5013525a  -> status=behind ahead_by=0 behind_by=1
# So e83d1997 is a STRICT DESCENDANT of the old pin by exactly one commit, and
# that commit is "fix(wiki): the host was eating the wiki's tab bar, not its
# header". Pinning 1b0a5013525a today ships the nav bug an ELEVENTH time.
#
# 🔴 ORDERING, and it is load-bearing: the host crop may only go to 0 because
# CM044 6b0492d is in the SHIPPED wiki image. Crop-0 without it re-opens
# c638a6d7 -- the black bar returns. That image was built and re-pinned in
# CM051 #1029 (site 4a7c6307, compiler 866e2312, both from CM044 6b0492d,
# release-images.yml success 16:31:24Z). Both halves are present in this cut
# or neither should be.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM051 names the tree whose install.sh SHIPS, compared by BLOB IDENTITY and
# not by ancestry. eb783851 is main at the moment this record was written. It
# carries all six walk fixes (#1027 #1028 #1026 #1018) and the wiki re-pin
# (#1029). The PR that adds this file touches cuts/ only -- NOT install.sh --
# so the blob it names is the blob that ships.
#
# Pins verified IN THE TREE, not from memory:
#   grep -c 'sha256:4a7c6307\|sha256:866e2312' install.sh  -> 2
#   wc -l install.sh                                       -> 25488  (control:
#   a truncated read greps 0 and reads exactly like "no pin")
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 THIS CUT IS BEING PUBLISHED UNWALKED, ON ANDY'S EXPLICIT INSTRUCTION.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-08-24 23:2xZ. The standing rule is that ostler.ai/install.dmg stays at
# v1.0.41 until a clean walk record exists, because a green cut repoints the
# public download automatically (board #844). Andy was shown that consequence
# in those words and chose to publish anyway. Recording it here so the next
# reader does not mistake it for the rule having changed, or for nobody having
# noticed. v1.0.45 has NO walk record at the moment it is published.
CUT_VERSION=1.0.45
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 🔴 PIN MOVED AGAIN, 2026-08-25: e83d1997ab18 -> c4c5b40b408e. READ THIS.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The first version of this file pinned e83d1997 and said, correctly, that it
# is the nav-crop fix. What it got WRONG was the PR number: I called it oa
# #341. It is oa #340. The BOM row said #340 all along -- the register was
# right and my report was wrong, and chasing that one-digit discrepancy is
# what surfaced the real defect.
#
#   oa #340  merged 2026-08-24T16:12:25Z  -> e83d1997  the nav crop
#   oa #341  merged 2026-08-24T16:30:56Z  -> c4c5b40b  board #877, the
#                                                      settings page had no
#                                                      way in
#
# MEASURED both directions:
#   c4c5b40b...e83d1997  status=behind  ahead=0 behind=1
#   e83d1997...c4c5b40b  status=ahead   ahead=1 behind=0
#
# So pinning e83d1997 shipped the crop fix and SILENTLY DROPPED #877 -- one of
# the walk findings this cut exists to close. Exactly the half-a-fix shape the
# crop itself had (wiki half without host half), one layer up. c4c5b40b is oa
# main and a strict descendant by one commit, so moving the pin gains #877 and
# loses nothing. The Hub app is rebuilt from it; the parity check in
# bin/cut.sh compares the app's embedded sha to the value below and will
# refuse if the two disagree.
DAEMON_COMMIT=c4c5b40b408e
CM051=eb78385115720c8d309870ab3d82d50243e101f9
